Which similarity test proves that these two triangles are similar?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.82]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.9,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.755,2.247);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,"$52^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,"$63^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=C--B--A};
\coordinate (A2) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (B2) at (8.75,0);
\coordinate (C2) at (7.033,3.37);
\draw (A2) -- (B2) -- (C2) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,"$52^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=B2--A2--C2};
\pic[draw,"$63^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.5cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=C2--B2--A2};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

